From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Martins <eduardo@martins.ws>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:16:14 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8015: Add spi1

The ADT's spi1 ("spi-1,samsung", spi-version 1) sits at 0x22e404000 with
IRQ 292 and the spi1 power domain. iBoot leaves its pins in their SPI
function. The iPhone X touch controller hangs off it.

Assisted-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015.dtsi | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015.dtsi
index 155adba20..cacf7e0c7 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015.dtsi
@@ -323,6 +323,18 @@ i2c3: i2c@22e20c000 {
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
+		spi1: spi@22e404000 {
+			compatible = "apple,t8015-spi", "apple,t8010-spi", "apple,spi";
+			reg = <0x2 0x2e404000 0x0 0x4000>;
+			interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
+			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 292 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			clocks = <&clkref>;
+			power-domains = <&ps_spi1>;
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		serial0: serial@22e600000 {
 			compatible = "apple,s5l-uart";
 			reg = <0x2 0x2e600000 0x0 0x4000>;
